      <h1>How Bitcoin Open-Source Projects Work</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin open-source projects include node software, wallets, Lightning implementations, libraries, hardware interfaces, developer tools, documentation, and infrastructure. Their source may be public, but each project has its own license, permissions, review process, release practices, funding, and maintenance risks.

Open source makes inspection, contribution, modification, and competition possible under the project’s license. It does not guarantee secure code, decentralized governance, active maintenance, reproducible binaries, compatibility, or adoption.</p>
